@BonkDaCarnivore People who think “no state income tax” is beneficial are delusional. 

With no income tax, localities must use property and sales taxes to raise revenue, and those are HIGHLY regressive

Texas property taxes are high so that the rich don’t have to pay income tax. Thats why.

Wow! Even Republicans are saying @GovHotWheels_TX is intentionally lying to voters about property taxes just to get re-elected.

"If the property tax system is broken, he’s had 12 years and Republican majorities in the legislature to fix it."

@dallasnews: https://t.co/Cow48EgNKY

@KalshiPolitics Outside of the Texas cities, some of the reddest counties were hit with HUGE property tax increases.  That is going to send a BIG amount of rural elderly people to the polls, and they are the most reliable voters anyway. They are going to be hit with bill increases in the hundreds to a thousand dollars.

And Texas is a state that is VICIOUS about property tax collection.  You don't pay, you WILL be thrown out on the street and it happens fast.

Republicans have a lock on the legislature and the governor's mansion but it's a different story and a far more mixed picture down at the bottom localities where these taxing authorities sit. This map does not work in Talarico's favor.
